00:05:57,272 --> 00:06:03,272
You don't have to be a hero to do this job. But it helps.

2
00:11:54,545 --> 00:12:00,545
The Hurt Locker is a drama, thriller, war film directed by Kathryn Bigelow.

3
00:17:51,818 --> 00:17:57,818
During the Iraq War, a Sergeant recently assigned to an army bomb squad is put at
odds with his squad mates due to his maverick way of handling his work.

4
00:23:49,090 --> 00:23:55,090
Staff Sergeant William James, played by Jeremy Renner.

5
00:29:46,363 --> 00:29:52,363
Sergeant JT Sanborn, played by Anthony Mackie.

6
00:35:43,636 --> 00:35:49,636
Specialist Owen Eldridge, played by Brian Geraghty.

7
00:41:40,909 --> 00:41:46,909
Colonel Reed, played by David Morse.

8
00:47:38,181 --> 00:47:44,181
Sergeant Matt Thompson, played by Guy Pearce.

9
00:53:35,454 --> 00:53:41,454
Connie James, played by Evangeline Lilly.

10
00:59:32,727 --> 00:59:38,727
The Hurt Locker is a 2008 American war film directed by
Kathryn Bigelow and written by Mark Boal.

11
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
It stars Jeremy Renner, Anthony Mackie, Brian Geraghty, Christian
Camargo, Ralph Fiennes, David Morse, and Guy Pearce.

12
01:11:27,272 --> 01:11:33,272
It follows an Iraq War bomb disposal team who are targeted by insurgents and
shows their psychological reactions to the stress of combat.

13
01:17:24,545 --> 01:17:30,545
Boal drew on his experience during embedded access to write the screenplay.

14
01:23:21,818 --> 01:23:27,818
The Hurt Locker premiered at the 2008 Venice International Film Festival and was
released in the United States on June 26, 2009, by Summit Entertainment.

15
01:29:19,090 --> 01:29:25,090
It received positive reviews from critics, who
praised the acting and cinematography.

16
01:35:16,363 --> 01:35:22,363
It was nominated for nine Academy Awards and won six, including Best Director and Best Original
Screenplay, and became the first film directed by a woman to win Best Picture.

17
01:41:13,636 --> 01:41:19,636
It grossed $50 million worldwide.

18
01:47:10,909 --> 01:47:16,909
The Hurt Locker is considered one of the most influential
war films of the 2000s and the 21st century.

19
01:53:08,181 --> 01:53:14,181
In 2020, it was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

20
01:59:05,454 --> 01:59:11,454
The film explores themes of rescue, sniper, explosive, loyalty, us army.

21
02:05:02,727 --> 02:05:08,727
The tone is emotional and intense.
